## Avatar Script

[INTRO - 0:00-0:35]
"Transformation requires investment, and investments require justification. Return on Investment – ROI – is the language executives and boards understand. In this video, I'll show you how to calculate, track, and communicate ROI for your transformation initiatives using Consultify's reporting tools."

[SECTION 1: Understanding Transformation ROI - 0:35-1:30]
"ROI measures the return you receive relative to what you invested. The basic formula is simple: ROI equals Net Benefit divided by Cost, expressed as a percentage.

But transformation ROI has nuances. Benefits often take time to materialize. Costs come upfront. Intangible benefits are real but hard to quantify.

Consultify helps you handle these complexities with structured ROI modeling that captures both tangible and intangible value, accounts for timing, and presents results in formats stakeholders trust."

[SECTION 2: Accessing ROI Tools - 1:30-2:15]
"ROI calculations are available in the Reports module. Click 'ROI Analysis' to access the tools.

You can analyze ROI at different levels: individual initiative, a group of related initiatives, an entire phase or wave, or your complete transformation program.

Select the scope you want to analyze. For most stakeholder discussions, program-level or phase-level ROI is most meaningful. Individual initiative ROI is useful for prioritization decisions."

[SECTION 3: Defining Benefits - 2:15-3:30]
"The first step is capturing benefits. Consultify structures benefits into categories:

Revenue benefits: New revenue streams, increased sales, improved pricing.

Cost benefits: Reduced labor costs, eliminated waste, lower technology costs, improved productivity.

Risk benefits: Avoided penalties, reduced insurance costs, prevented losses.

Strategic benefits: Competitive advantage, market positioning, capability building.

For each benefit, enter the expected value, timing (when it starts and how long it lasts), and confidence level. Confidence adjusts the calculation – a 50% confidence benefit counts half.

Link benefits back to initiatives. This creates traceability – you can show which initiatives drive which benefits."

[SECTION 4: Tracking Costs - 3:30-4:30]
"Next, capture all costs. Categories include:

Implementation costs: Labor, consulting, software, hardware, training, change management.

Ongoing costs: Licenses, support, maintenance, additional headcount.

Transition costs: Productivity losses during changeover, parallel running costs.

Enter actual or estimated costs per initiative. As implementation progresses, update estimates with actuals for more accurate ROI tracking.

Cost timing matters too. Upfront costs hit hard; spread costs are easier to absorb. The model accounts for when costs are incurred."

[SECTION 5: ROI Calculation - 4:30-5:30]
"With benefits and costs entered, Consultify calculates several ROI metrics:

Simple ROI: Net benefit divided by cost. Easy to understand, but doesn't account for timing.

Net Present Value (NPV): Benefits and costs discounted to today's value. Shows the total value creation in current terms.

Internal Rate of Return (IRR): The effective interest rate your investment earns. Useful for comparing against cost of capital or alternative investments.

Payback Period: How long until cumulative benefits exceed cumulative costs. Answers 'when do we break even?'

The ROI dashboard displays all these metrics with visualizations showing benefit and cost flows over time."

[SECTION 6: Scenario Modeling - 5:30-6:15]
"ROI projections involve uncertainty. Consultify supports scenario analysis.

Create optimistic, baseline, and pessimistic scenarios by adjusting benefit assumptions or confidence levels. See how ROI changes under different conditions.

Sensitivity analysis shows which assumptions most affect ROI. If your ROI depends heavily on one benefit assumption, you know where to focus validation efforts.

Monte Carlo simulation (available in Enterprise plans) runs thousands of scenarios to provide probability distributions – not just single ROI numbers, but likely ranges."

[SECTION 7: Communicating ROI - 6:15-6:40]
"Numbers alone aren't compelling. Consultify generates ROI presentations combining metrics with context.

The executive summary highlights key figures: total investment, total expected return, ROI percentage, payback period. One slide, all key facts.

Detailed breakdowns show benefit and cost components for those who want to dig deeper.

Charts show the investment curve – costs going out, benefits coming in – painting the picture of transformation value over time."

[OUTRO - 6:40-7:00]
"ROI is how you prove transformation value. Build the model early, update it regularly, and communicate it clearly. Your stakeholders will thank you.

In the final video, we'll learn how to create executive summary reports that bring together all your transformation insights for leadership review. Let's finish strong!"

